{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2300 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e6340217f9cc39206f1293ed1b7f89f4042396e4860c2b2fbe65987a010ea0f2" :edb/db-before-t 2299 :edb/db-after-t 2300 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535612 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:36:12.122Z" 13194139535612 true] [17592186133762 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357536 13194139535612 true] [17592186133763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357529 13194139535612 true] [17592186133764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357515 13194139535612 true] [17592186133764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357522 13194139535612 true] [17592186134119 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535612 true] [17592186134119 1100 "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy.$" 13194139535612 true] [17592186134119 1100 "Calculate $∫_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{π/2}}∫_{0}^{y^{2}}\\sin y^{3}dxdy$." 13194139535612 false] [17592186134119 1145 "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357515 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357516 13194139535612 true] [17592186357515 1089 "q-132529" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357515 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535612 true] [17592186357515 1100 "Calculate ${∬}_{D}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dA,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-y\\le x\\le 2y}.$" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357515 1113 #uuid "d5f009be-0871-5507-bce4-956000cf9505" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357515 1145 "The integral is defined over a type II region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-y\\le x\\le 2y}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-y}^{2y}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-y}^{2y}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}[{\\int }_{-y}^{2y}x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{-y}^{2y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}(2{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dy & =\\frac{1}{2}{[{e}^{{y}^{3}}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357517 13194139535612 true] [17592186357516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357518 13194139535612 true] [17592186357516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357519 13194139535612 true] [17592186357516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357520 13194139535612 true] [17592186357516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357521 13194139535612 true] [17592186357516 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535612 true] [17592186357516 1041 "selection" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357516 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357520 13194139535612 true] [17592186357516 1110 #uuid "be3eee5a-bd68-599e-be5e-bf211f2309c2" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357517 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{4}+2)" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357517 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357517 1111 #uuid "0ba4d452-09ce-5907-9a59-c3ebde4b6bad" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357518 1034 "{e}^{8}-1" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357518 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357518 1111 #uuid "58bbe423-9a00-5f5b-a460-1b71dc97d41c" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357519 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}+2)" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357519 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357519 1111 #uuid "d5c12d64-7969-5e82-a624-258c1adab26b" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357520 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357520 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357520 1111 #uuid "791b381d-0c08-5c83-81ef-983fd6187469" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357521 1034 "{e}^{4}-1" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357521 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357521 1111 #uuid "f147fce4-7d29-558a-8458-ba7e7ea536e5" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357522 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357523 13194139535612 true] [17592186357522 1089 "q-132563" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357522 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535612 true] [17592186357522 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/e15621dd6402a86de5c5d172880c7cbdc2a933e852259ad81d5ebcf9a89b9984.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}2x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10$ and $y=2x+1,$ above the line $y=1,$ as shown in the picture." 13194139535612 true] [17592186357522 1113 #uuid "0d937870-20e3-5ed3-ad6f-56e0cffb3636" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357522 1145 "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}} \\\\ y=2x+1 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(y-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y-1) \\\\ 2\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}} & =y-1 \\\\ (2\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}})^{2} & =(y-1)^{2} \\\\ 40-4{y}^{2} & ={y}^{2}-2y+1 \\\\ 5{y}^{2}-2y-39 & =0 \\\\ (5y+13)(y-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the line $y=1$, the $y$-limits are \n$1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/33487fff6ff0b0e74bab4e6d6acdcb6902d40e938525d7de92d684ed5d98273a.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(y-1)\\le x\\le \\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}2x\\,dA={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}2x\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}2x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}2x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{x}^{2}]_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(10-{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(y-1)^{2})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(10-{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(y-1)^{2})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(10-{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(y-1)^{2})dy & ={[10y-\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{12}(y-1)^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(30-9-\\frac{2}{3})-(10-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{61}{3}-\\frac{29}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357523 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357524 13194139535612 true] [17592186357523 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357525 13194139535612 true] [17592186357523 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357526 13194139535612 true] [17592186357523 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357527 13194139535612 true] [17592186357523 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357528 13194139535612 true] [17592186357523 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535612 true] [17592186357523 1041 "selection" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357523 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357527 13194139535612 true] [17592186357523 1110 #uuid "494e7700-d265-5332-b3ff-cc8e557a559d" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357524 1034 "13" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357524 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357524 1111 #uuid "0273b340-18ee-5c3c-bf39-48af0b32763c" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357525 1034 "11" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357525 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357525 1111 #uuid "19a872e1-08f8-5352-a1b6-d44f10bed845" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357526 1034 "\\frac{25}{3}" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357526 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357526 1111 #uuid "c6086d76-32de-51ed-bd89-d80000f6b1a7" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357527 1034 "\\frac{32}{3}" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357527 1111 #uuid "f11f6044-a28f-5ff6-9cbe-f5e82f2b8b16" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357528 1034 "\\frac{7}{3}" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357528 1111 #uuid "43ed516f-e22e-55e6-ad32-b94c7c7e22b4" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357529 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357530 13194139535612 true] [17592186357529 1089 "q-37685" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357529 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535612 true] [17592186357529 1100 "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy.$" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357529 1113 #uuid "699935ac-2009-58b3-9525-0eee26e7f93b" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357529 1145 "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{y}^{1}dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}[x]_{y}^{1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}(1-y)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{y}{1+{y}^{2}})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{y}{1+{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{2})}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{1}^{2})}{2}-(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{0}^{2})}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357530 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357531 13194139535612 true] [17592186357530 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357532 13194139535612 true] [17592186357530 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357533 13194139535612 true] [17592186357530 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357534 13194139535612 true] [17592186357530 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357535 13194139535612 true] [17592186357530 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535612 true] [17592186357530 1041 "selection" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357530 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357535 13194139535612 true] [17592186357530 1110 #uuid "5b23e53b-7f93-5056-a771-c9d32a10fe9d" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357531 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357531 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357531 1111 #uuid "f80c770c-bcc9-5f93-a3e3-948113c20170" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357532 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357532 1111 #uuid "f1d195e6-e0ea-5864-8b8d-4ad59c0ebc8f" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357533 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357533 1111 #uuid "68f8b43f-8af8-50e1-b275-c7306bf5b0bc" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357534 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357534 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357534 1111 #uuid "deab1e46-423d-5377-a7db-718db1f3ec89" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357535 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357535 1111 #uuid "dcb4a4e1-8d2e-5332-b9fa-45abd01cf471" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357536 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357537 13194139535612 true] [17592186357536 1089 "q-40581" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357536 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535612 true] [17592186357536 1100 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curves $y=x-2,$ and $y=\\sqrt{x},$ above the $x$-axis. What is ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA\\,$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357536 1113 #uuid "362fcf20-6d09-5e57-8338-b11857a062d4" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357536 1145 "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/6817e13f2f4c019f337425bd9f2284386c7077c0ac97da51fc26fdea19f8ee67.png)\n\nWe need to represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=x-2$ and $y=\\sqrt{x}$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=x-2 & \\,⟹\\,x=y+2 \\\\ y=\\sqrt{x} & \\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =y+2 \\\\ {y}^{2}-y-2 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)(y+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/db9d1846b19b75a629ad0a0d4b6e138aa2cef91cd8c0324a9285ed9c44befb60.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le y+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357538 13194139535612 true] [17592186357537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357539 13194139535612 true] [17592186357537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357540 13194139535612 true] [17592186357537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357541 13194139535612 true] [17592186357537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357542 13194139535612 true] [17592186357537 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535612 true] [17592186357537 1041 "selection" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357537 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357538 13194139535612 true] [17592186357537 1110 #uuid "7d5b1079-3494-53a8-b6e9-5cb48aa9323e" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357538 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357538 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357538 1111 #uuid "6991940d-1769-5e65-9d9b-a0829ca8976d" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357539 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y-2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357539 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535612 true] [17592186357539 1111 #uuid "a6743543-f257-5acb-be74-a00c26cc37d8" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357540 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{-y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139535612 true] [17592186357540 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1